{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are ThreadSense grounding verifier. You verify independently of the drafting agent; you judge and never repair.\nYour personal goal is: Judge every statement against the full topic context and decide whether the passed premises justify the exact proposed action."},{"role":"user","content":"\nCurrent Task: Judge each statement against the evidence it cites, read within the full context provided: every message of every member thread (with canonical author IDs, roles, thread starters and reactions) and every retrieved source for this topic. Citing a source is not support. A statement is SUPPORTED only if its cited evidence states or directly entails it and nothing in the context contradicts it; PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED if a material part is missing or the context qualifies it; UNSUPPORTED otherwise. A status line marking an excerpt historical, unresolved or a prior record means it cannot support what applies now. By kind: CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT is a report of what members say, not a verified cause; CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT is SUPPORTED if the cited source says it, described with its status and dates; it establishes no current handling, procedure or destination; CLAIM_CAUSE needs verification in the cited evidence; a Verbatim quote must match its source, a Paraphrase must preserve the meaning. Prose names no one: role wording (\"the team lead instructs\", \"a tutor reports\") must match the cited author's role and act (reported, asked, confirmed or instructed), plural wording needs that many distinct cited authors, and listed attributions must hold (AUTHOR wrote the cited message, THREAD_STARTER started its thread, PARTICIPANT posted in it). A retrieved record's authorship is separate from its authority: an approver or recorder (actor_relation RECORD_AUTHORITY) is not its author, and a record whose authorship is not verified names no author. SUMMARY and SEVERITY_RATIONALE must follow from the evidence with no added cause, count or outcome. A SUMMARY sentence (statement_id summary:s1, summary:s2, ...) is judged on its own and shown only if SUPPORTED; its attributions name the people its role wording refers to, and wording that groups several people is SUPPORTED only if what it says they asked or reported is stated in each of their cited messages. A SUMMARY sentence with depends_on is read after the sentences it lists (for words such as \"this\" or \"their\"), but judged only on what it adds. A DETAIL sentence (statement_id detail:d1, detail:d2, ...) is shown when the card is opened and is judged exactly like a SUMMARY sentence: on its own, shown only if SUPPORTED, read after the sentences in its depends_on but judged only on what it adds. NO_ACTION_RATIONALE is the advisor's reason for proposing no further intervention now: SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence shows that reason and the context shows no unresolved handling question, guidance gap, applicable pending decision or operational problem that needs coordination; existing guidance does not by itself establish that no action is needed. ACTION and ALTERNATIVE are recommendations: judge whether their premises are supported, whether the action applies to this topic and whether the rationale follows; a source need not literally prescribe the action. Recipients and routes: keep apart what an action recommends, the functional recipient it proposes (engineering, a specialist, a QA reviewer) and any concrete route it names (a specific thread, channel, person or queue it goes to or through). A proposed functional recipient is justified by supported incident evidence showing a problem that needs that recipient's expertise; evidence of an established intake route is not required, and mentioning the recipient justifies nothing by itself. A concrete route, or a claim that a route is designated, official or mandatory, is a claim of its own and needs a premise whose evidence establishes it; an example-collection or status note asks people where to post examples and does not make that thread an intake route. The recommendation stays advisory (the team lead decides; it need not be shown to be the required or only next step): when no evidence names the concrete route, leave it unspecified (\"report it to engineering\") rather than choosing one. Judge a proposed recipient the same way in ACTION, ALTERNATIVE, INTERVENTION_NEED, ACTION_RATIONALE and REVIEW_NOTE: on whether the incident evidence shows a problem that needs that recipient's expertise, never on whether an intake route is on record; a statement that proposes a recipient and leaves the concrete route unspecified is not PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED, UNSUPPORTED or insufficient for that reason. ACTION and operational ALTERNATIVE statements list their premises: PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT premises are judged here and are provisional, not final; REJECTED ones failed deterministic checks and support nothing; a premise with depends_on stands only if every ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING statement it lists is also SUPPORTED. ACTION_CHOICE is SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence really leaves that choice between the named actions open (not merely an imagined alternative, a review flag or an unknown cause). INTERVENTION_NEED says why intervening now is needed: SUPPORTED only if the context shows that reason (an unresolved handling question, a guidance gap, an applicable pending decision, or an operational problem that needs coordination). Questions already answered in their threads are not unresolved; a general benefit (\"a reminder might help\") is not a need; existing guidance does not by itself rule a need out. Judge in this order: (1) announcement handling; (2) each premise's final status, which is your verdict on it combined with its dependencies; (3) sufficiency. Fill action_sufficiency for the ACTION and one alternative_sufficiency entry (with its statement_id) for each ALTERNATIVE that lists premises: SUFFICIENT only if premises whose final status is SUPPORTED justify the exact text as worded, including its conditions and scope; essential_statement_ids lists the premises it cannot stand without (each must have final status SUPPORTED); INSUFFICIENT if its exact text relies on a rejected, unsupported or dependency-voided premise or goes beyond its premises; a listed premise the text does not rely on is not essential, and its failure alone does not make the action insufficient. ACTION_RATIONALE is judged separately and may also cite context claims; action_sufficiency null if no ACTION statement is sent. SOURCE_AGREEMENT is SUPPORTED only if the named current sources say the same thing on the point in conflict and only the superseded material differs. A request by anyone but a team lead is a CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT: SUPPORTED if that person asked it, and it carries no authority. CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION is a team lead's in-thread instruction: SUPPORTED only if that message gives it and it applies to the threads in scope; it is not project guidance. HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE needs retrieved records of earlier occurrences; REPORTED_RECURRENCE only needs members saying it is happening again. AFFECTED_REPORTER needs that person's own message reporting that they are affected. RESOLUTION is judged against the member's complete thread, including messages the statement did not cite. ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING needs the announcement to give that directive for this topic's project, batch and problem, and it governs only what it directs (a request to post examples governs where examples go, not escalation or an intake route); a routine reminder or schedule directs nothing for the topic. OPEN_QUESTION is SUPPORTED only if the guidance and decisions in the context really leave that specific question unsettled and it is a handling or policy question for the team lead; a not-yet-diagnosed cause, pending diagnostic results or a pending expert assessment is not one. Return exactly one verdict for every statement_id. The team lead reads SUMMARY, DETAIL, ACTION (label, instruction, draft to copy, scope and changes), ACTION_RATIONALE, NO_ACTION_RATIONALE, REVIEW_NOTE and OPEN_QUESTION exactly as written: judge that exact text, including its conditions, uncertainty, scope and who reported, asked, confirmed or instructed; plain wording is expected, but it must not overstate the evidence. A quoted passage must match its source exactly. open_review_flags lists the upstream review obligations still open on these threads; a REVIEW_NOTE may rely on them. Source consistency (always fill source_consistency, even when the draft declares no conflict): compare the governing_sources that address the handling question of this topic with each other, independently of the draft. List sources that state the same rule as AGREE, and sources that state different rules for the same cases as CONFLICT with the point and disagreement_scope (which cases, batch or section differ). assessed_evidence_ids lists the governing sources you compared; relations may be empty when they address different points. Only governing sources count: historical, superseded, expired or withdrawn material, prior records and member messages are not current sources, an announcement governs only if it directs handling for this topic, and members disagreeing with each other is not a source conflict. For each entry in declared_conflicts give one declared_conflict_checks entry: CONFIRMED (the cited sources state different rules on that point), SOURCES_AGREE (they say the same thing; only wording or detail differs) or UNDETERMINED.\n\nInput JSON:\n{\"topic\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_15\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_e1fd3fe0ab51eb4c\", \"topic_id\": \"cluster_e1fd3fe0ab51eb4c/topic_1\", \"topic_label\": \"Rubric version conflict\", \"projection_gap\": null, \"as_of\": \"2026-10-02T12:00:00Z\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_92efb4b634ca03e5a5d0f8d8\", \"member_c55df1c33b1835f1c0d3d4a2\"]}, \"statements\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor asks which version of the error rubric is valid now.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790893703.000042\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U017\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790893703.000042\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports that an older scoring screenshot seems to disagree with a newer pinned note.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790893759.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U015\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790893759.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports that a rubric example differs from Friday's alignment and asks whether the later announcement replaces the older note, citing RP-4295.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894295.000041\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U020\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894295.000041\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks which wording appears in the current pinned message and which appears in the archived screenshot in the RP-4295 thread.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894342.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894342.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION\", \"text\": \"In the RP-4295 thread, the team lead requests both versions and their dates and declines to declare either document superseded until the change history is verified. Verbatim quote: \\\"Please attach both versions and their dates. I am not declaring either document superseded until we verify the change history.\\\"\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894390.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894390.000226\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT\", \"text\": \"The current instructions provide a content-quality rubric, but the retrieved excerpt does not identify the reported screenshot or pinned note or establish their supersession.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:a71c54c7\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_HISTORY\", \"text\": \"The September 16 tie-calibration approval covers a batch-14 exercise rather than a policy change; at that record's cutoff, posting was pending and an outcome had not been observed.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:rp-tie-calibration-approval@1.0:99b5da48\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c8\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INFERENCE\", \"text\": \"The first tutor's thread contains a version question and a reported discrepancy, but no answer identifying which version is valid.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790893703.000042\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790893759.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U017\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790893703.000042\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U015\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790893759.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c9\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INFERENCE\", \"text\": \"The RP-4295 thread ends with the team lead's request; the requested versions and dates have not been provided in that thread.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894295.000041\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894342.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894390.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894390.000226\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c10\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_HISTORY\", \"text\": \"The September 20 batch-14 follow-up records completed tie calibration and improved agreement in the reviewed sample; it concerns the same sampled pairs and does not record a rubric-version replacement.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:rp-tie-calibration-outcome@1.0:f678161f\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c11\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT\", \"text\": \"The team lead's September 29 announcement directs a JSON format for batch-15 weekly QA audit manifests and explicitly states that this administrative handoff format does not change model-response comparisons or settle accuracy-versus-format tradeoffs.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:rp-audit-manifest-post@1.0:f64eba9c\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"k:rp-audit-manifest-post@1.0:f64eba9c\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c12\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_HISTORY\", \"text\": \"The September 25 audit-manifest approval concerns combining QA handoff files, leaves existing task ratings and rationales unchanged, and records no posted draft or checked converted export at that cutoff.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:rp-audit-manifest-approval@1.0:41e2a032\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s1\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"Two tutors ask which rubric version applies, including whether a later announcement replaces an older note.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790893703.000042\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894295.000041\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U017\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790893703.000042\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U020\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894295.000041\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s2\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"In the RP-4295 thread, the team lead has deferred any supersession decision until both versions, their dates and the change history can be checked.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894390.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894390.000226\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d1\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports that an older scoring screenshot seems to disagree with a newer pinned note in the first thread, which contains no answer identifying the valid version.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790893759.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790893703.000042\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U015\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790893759.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U017\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790893703.000042\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d2\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The tutor asking about RP-4295 reports a difference between a rubric example and Friday's alignment.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894295.000041\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U020\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894295.000041\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d3\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor in the RP-4295 thread asks which wording appears in the current pinned message and which appears in the archived screenshot.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894342.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894342.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d4\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The RP-4295 thread does not include the versions and dates requested by the team lead.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894295.000041\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894342.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894390.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894390.000226\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d5\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The earlier batch-14 tie-calibration approval was not a policy change; a later follow-up records completed calibration and improved agreement in the reviewed sample, not a rubric-version replacement.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:rp-tie-calibration-approval@1.0:99b5da48\", \"k:rp-tie-calibration-outcome@1.0:f678161f\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d6\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The September 29 audit announcement concerns JSON files for weekly QA handoffs and explicitly does not change how model responses are compared.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:rp-audit-manifest-post@1.0:f64eba9c\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U001\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"k:rp-audit-manifest-post@1.0:f64eba9c\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:no_action\", \"kind\": \"NO_ACTION_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Why no further action is needed now: The team lead has already requested the comparison inputs and deferred a decision in that thread. Those inputs have not been supplied there, so the pending check does not yet call for another instruction.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790893703.000042\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894295.000041\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894390.000226\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894342.000113\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:a71c54c7\", \"k:rp-tie-calibration-approval@1.0:99b5da48\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790893759.000113\", \"k:rp-tie-calibration-outcome@1.0:f678161f\", \"k:rp-audit-manifest-post@1.0:f64eba9c\", \"k:rp-audit-manifest-approval@1.0:41e2a032\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_92efb4b634ca03e5a5d0f8d8\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_92efb4b634ca03e5a5d0f8d8 is UNRESOLVED: The tutor asks which version is valid, and a tutor replies with an apparent discrepancy rather than an answer.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790893703.000042\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790893759.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_c55df1c33b1835f1c0d3d4a2\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_c55df1c33b1835f1c0d3d4a2 is UNRESOLVED: The tutor's supersession question remains unanswered; a QA tutor asks for wording and the team lead defers a decision pending versions, dates and change-history verification.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894295.000041\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894342.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894390.000226\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:rationale\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Severity MEDIUM: Two tutors report apparent disagreements between scoring materials, including one tied to RP-4295. These reports suggest meaningful scoring uncertainty, but do not establish widespread incorrect scoring or an inability to complete work.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790893759.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894295.000041\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790893703.000042\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894342.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:signal:MEDIUM[1]\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_SIGNAL\", \"text\": \"Rubric signal met - \\\"Conflicting interpretations that affect, or are reasonably likely to affect, how tasks are scored or handled\\\": A tutor reports disagreement between an older scoring screenshot and a newer pinned note; a tutor separately reports that a rubric example differs from Friday's alignment on RP-4295.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790893759.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894295.000041\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"reporter:U015\", \"kind\": \"AFFECTED_REPORTER\", \"text\": \"U015 reports, in their own cited message, being affected by this problem.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790893759.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"reporter:U020\", \"kind\": \"AFFECTED_REPORTER\", \"text\": \"U020 reports, in their own cited message, being affected by this problem.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894295.000041\"]}], \"member_threads\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790893703.000042\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_92efb4b634ca03e5a5d0f8d8\", \"thread_id\": \"1790893703.000042\", \"author_id\": \"U017\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T22:28:23.000042Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U017\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Anyone else seeing this? Which version of the error rubric is valid now?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790893759.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_92efb4b634ca03e5a5d0f8d8\", \"thread_id\": \"1790893703.000042\", \"author_id\": \"U015\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T22:29:19.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U017\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"The older scoring screenshot seems to disagree with the newer pinned note.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894295.000041\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_c55df1c33b1835f1c0d3d4a2\", \"thread_id\": \"1790894295.000041\", \"author_id\": \"U020\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T22:38:15.000041Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U020\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Task check: The example in the rubric says one thing, but Friday's alignment says another. Can we check whether the later announcement replaces the older note? (task ref RP-4295)\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894342.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_c55df1c33b1835f1c0d3d4a2\", \"thread_id\": \"1790894295.000041\", \"author_id\": \"U002\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T22:39:02.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U020\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Which wording appears in the current pinned message and which in the archived screenshot?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790894390.000226\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_c55df1c33b1835f1c0d3d4a2\", \"thread_id\": \"1790894295.000041\", \"author_id\": \"U001\", \"author_role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T22:39:50.000226Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U020\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Please attach both versions and their dates. I am not declaring either document superseded until we verify the change history.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"THREAD_SCOPE\"}], \"retrieved_sources\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:a71c54c7\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-instructions@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — Instructions (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Content-quality rubric\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Content-quality rubric\\nMajor/minor describe task-quality defects and do not determine operational incident severity.\\n\\n| Dimension | Major defect | Minor defect | Acceptable / no automatic penalty |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| Factual accuracy | Error changes the central conclusion or actionable answer | Nonessential background error without that effect | Accurate paraphrase or an immaterial stylistic difference |\\n| Instruction adherence | Explicit required format/structure is missing | Limited violation of an actual secondary requirement | A stylistic choice that violates no requirement |\\n| Citation support | Fabricated reference or materially unsupported attribution | A limited citation-detail error where the source and support remain identifiable | A valid source that supports the claim |\\n| Preference | Identify a meaningful benefit; grade underlying defects separately | Do not manufacture a defect to break a tie | No meaningful quality difference supports a tie |\\n\\nAn inaccessible link needs a verification note; lack of access alone does not establish the error grade of the claim.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:slack:C_RP_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790888971.000030:7db831c7\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"ANNOUNCEMENT\", \"citation\": {\"title\": \"Slack announcement in response-preference-announcements at 2026-10-01T21:09:31.000030+00:00\", \"source\": {\"channel_id\": \"C_RP_ANNOUNCEMENTS\", \"message_id\": \"1790888971.000030\", \"system\": \"slack\", \"thread_id\": \"1790888971.000030\"}}, \"source_type\": \"announcement\", \"record_kind\": \"announcement\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-10-01T21:09:31.000030+00:00\", \"basis\": \"created_at\", \"created_at\": \"2026-10-01T21:09:31.000030+00:00\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_15\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"same_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"MESSAGE_AUTHOR\", \"ap