\"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Tool incidents and submission\\nIf response panes never load, record a fetch incident and do not infer response quality. If Submit fails, capture the task ID, required-field state, error and exact button behavior. A selected label is not a completed submission until LT confirms it. Assess tool impact separately from the content rubric.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:fa9b6a3d\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-faq@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — FAQ (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Instruction following\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-faq\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"faq\", \"record_kind\": \"faq\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-05T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-05T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Instruction following\\n\\n### Q: The prompt required JSON, but one response is well-written prose. Which response wins?\\nThe required format is not optional: record its violation separately from factual accuracy. No universal tie-break rule is established for competing accuracy and instruction-following defects. If the actual pair and applicable guidance do not settle the preference, provide the prompt and both responses for TL confirmation.\\n\\n### Q: Can accuracy outweigh ignoring a requested output structure?\\nScore the dimensions separately and identify whether the requested structure was mandatory. Do not infer a general priority rule from one example or decide without the other response's evidence.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:rp-audit-manifest-post@1.0:f64eba9c\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"ANNOUNCEMENT\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"rp-audit-manifest-post@1.0\", \"title\": \"Weekly audit manifest convention communicated\", \"source\": {\"channel_id\": \"C_RP_ANNOUNCEMENTS\", \"message_id\": \"1790690400.810002\", \"system\": \"slack\", \"thread_id\": \"1790690400.810002\"}}, \"source_type\": \"announcement\", \"record_kind\": \"channel_announcement\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"history\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-29T14:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-29T14:00:00Z\", \"created_at\": \"2026-09-29T14:00:00.810002+00:00\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_15\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"same_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"MESSAGE_AUTHOR\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_slack_archive\"}, \"authorship\": {\"author_id\": \"U001\", \"verified\": true, \"basis\": \"SLACK_MESSAGE_AUTHOR\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"tl_approved\", \"decision_status\": \"tl_approved\", \"execution_status\": \"posted\", \"outcome_status\": \"not_observed\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[ANNOUNCEMENT posted 2026-09-29T14:00:00Z by TEAM_LEAD (rp_batch_15): not established as handling for this topic until you show it is relevant and gives a directive.]\\nFor RP batch 15 weekly QA audit exports prepared from today, the manifest must be JSON rather than a prose list. Use the fields batch_id, audit_date, and task_ids, and name the file rp15_audit_YYYY-MM-DD.json. This is an administrative handoff format for QA files. It does not change how we compare the model responses in a task or settle any accuracy-versus-format tradeoff in those responses.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:slack:C_RP_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790871613.000001:430efd10\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"ANNOUNCEMENT\", \"citation\": {\"title\": \"Slack announcement in response-preference-announcements at 2026-10-01T16:20:13.000001+00:00\", \"source\": {\"channel_id\": \"C_RP_ANNOUNCEMENTS\", \"message_id\": \"1790871613.000001\", \"system\": \"slack\", \"thread_id\": \"1790871613.000001\"}}, \"source_type\": \"announcement\", \"record_kind\": \"announcement\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"history\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-10-01T16:20:13.000001+00:00\", \"basis\": \"created_at\", \"created_at\": \"2026-10-01T16:20:13.000001+00:00\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_15\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"same_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"MESSAGE_AUTHOR\", \"approval_status\": \"UNKNOWN\"}, \"authorship\": {\"author_id\": \"U001\", \"verified\": true, \"basis\": \"SLACK_MESSAGE_AUTHOR\"}, \"upstream_review\": {\"review_required\": true, \"review_reasons\": [\"It is correct that no scoring method is supplied, but Avery does provide an example of misleading citation support: the source exists while its quoted paragraph addresses another claim. The rationale incorrectly says no examples were provided.\"]}, \"excerpt\": \"[ANNOUNCEMENT posted 2026-10-01T16:20:13.000001+00:00 by TEAM_LEAD (rp_batch_15): not established as handling for this topic until you show it is relevant and gives a directive.]\\nBatch status note — How to score responses with weak, missing, or misleading citations. Please keep examples in this thread while we check the scope.\\n\\nContext reply [1790871661.000113] by U010 (TUTOR):\\nThe source is real, but the quoted paragraph is about a different claim.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:rp-audit-manifest-approval@1.0:41e2a032\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"PRIOR_DECISION\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"rp-audit-manifest-approval@1.0\", \"title\": \"Approve a JSON format for weekly audit manifests\", \"sections\": [\"Evidence available at review\", \"Prior ThreadSense advice\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"rp-audit-manifest-approval\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"decision\", \"record_kind\": \"advice_review\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"history\", \"enactment\": {\"status\": \"NOT_ENACTED\", \"missing\": [\"NOT_A_POLICY_CHANGE\"]}}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-25T15:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-25T15:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_15\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"same_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"tl_approved\", \"decision_status\": \"tl_approved\", \"execution_status\": \"not_executed\", \"outcome_status\": \"not_observed\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[RELATED RECORD - not a search match: recorded forward link from rp-audit-manifest-post; series link from rp-audit-manifest-post.]\\n[PRIOR RECORD (advice_review; decision_status: tl_approved; execution_status: not_executed; outcome_status: not_observed) - history, not a standing rule.]\\n## Evidence available a